their neighbour holds.  Taking the lower-numbered fork first breaks the circle:
the last philosopher reaches first for the fork the first one wants.
␀The dining philosophers: %u tasks at a table, a fork (a mutex) between each two.
␀%u philosophers ate %u meals (%u to %u each); a fork was in two hands %u times.
␀Each takes the lower-numbered of their forks first.  Ctrl-C ends it.
␀Each takes the fork on their left first (-d).  Ctrl-C ends it.
␀philo: can't find myself (/bin/%s, ./%s, /rom/sample/c/%s)
␀usage: philo [-d] [-n MEALS] [PHILOSOPHERS]   (2-5)
␀
  philosopher  task  doing     forks  meals
␀philo: %u tasks free, not %u (philo %u)
␀no segment or semaphore␀/rom/sample/c/␀  %-11s  %4u
␀
  held by 
