count when it ran again, and the adds the others had made meanwhile were lost.
The mutex lets one task at a time between the read and the write: the others
wait for it, using no CPU.
␀race: %u tasks share a counter, and each adds 1 to it %u times:
␀race: can't find myself (/bin/%s, ./%s, /rom/sample/c/%s)
␀usage: race [TASKS [ADDS]]   (TASKS 1-5, ADDS 1-5000)
␀reads it, works a little, and writes it back plus one␀  the counter: %u of %u: %u adds lost (%u.%u s)[K␀  the counter: %u of %u: none lost (%u.%u s)[K␀With a mutex around each read and write:␀With nothing to keep them apart:␀  the counter: %u (stopped)[K␀no segment or semaphore␀  task %-2u [%*s] %5u␀  the counter: 0␀/rom/sample/c/␀ no task free
␀interrupted␀no workers␀[%u;%uH␀[H[2J␀usage␀%s[K␀/bin/␀race␀./␀-w␀%u␀±3¼3_30123456789ABCDEF-2147483648␀␀	
